  "Assumptions": {
    "Selection": "First row-major feature cell; replace its entire cardinal component. Rubble keeps one model; heavy debris uses the existing connected 3x3 partition",
    "Footprint": "Rubble keeps its established footprint. HeavyDebris composes one body and up to two separate fragments per connected patch; fragment centres stay on occupied cells. Irregular occupied cells remain the gameplay footprint",
    "GroundScale": "HeavyDebris scales each body or fragment uniformly in XYZ, including PlanarFit, then applies its rotation and the grid Y stretch of sqrt(2). Long and large patches are composed from separate pieces instead of stretching one object",
    "Variety": "Stable spatial anchor chooses the body variant and turn; heavy debris retains the existing furniture/console/rack/canopy families. VariantOverride only stages an explicit visual comparison",
    "Height": "Rubble: established source Z multiplied by min(2, XY scale). HeavyDebris: same scale as source X and Y before the grid stretch",
    "Clip": "idle at zero seconds",
    "SimulationUnchanged": true
  }
